  "id": "Compound::DB00726 - Gene::6532",
  "verbalization": "Trimipramine is associated with Slc6a4 through a series of molecular and pharmacological interactions. The evidence suggests that Trimipramine, a tricyclic antidepressant, induces the condition Taste Peculiar, which is linked to Protriptyline or Trazodone. Both Protriptyline and Trazodone bind to Slc6a4, a gene involved in ion transport and neurotransmitter regulation. This indicates that Trimipramine may influence Slc6a4 through the activation of these secondary mediators, potentially altering the function of the Slc6a4 protein. The shared lowest common ancestors, Tricyclic Antidepressant and Organic Tricyclic Compound, further support a common pharmacological pathway involving these compounds. The evidence suggests a possible role of Trimipramine in modulating Slc6a4 activity, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
